From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 15:03:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] dzn: export onyx_set_log_hook and report D3D12 failures

Release builds of Dozen fail silently: most D3D12 HRESULTs are dropped and
turned into VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY. For the UWP (Xbox Dev Mode) port:

- export onyx_set_log_hook() so the application can receive Mesa's log
  (sets g_mesa_log_hook, see the util patch) via GetProcAddress;
- log every failed D3D12 object creation, OpenSharedHandle, queue
  Signal/Wait and command list Close with its HRESULT, plus the device
  removed reason when the device is gone (DZN_HR wrapper);
- log root signature serialization errors with the error blob;
- give nir_to_dxil a logger (its default one hits UNREACHABLE, undefined
  behaviour in release builds) and always log DXIL validation failures,
  even without diagnostics from dxcompiler.dll;
- refuse to execute command buffers whose recording failed, which would
  remove the D3D12 device shared with the rest of the process, and check
  the device removed reason after every ExecuteCommandLists;
- log a line when the instance and the device are created.
